      "id": "CASE-0090",
      "name": "Money laundering",
      "status": "ACTIVE",
      "priority": "HIGH",
      "description": "This report details suspected financial fraud, coordinated logistics, and communications involving existing entities and newly identified individuals and locations. A significant financial transfer to an account linked to Northstar Logistics Ltd. is noted, followed by related movements and a meeting at a new storage facility.",
      "brief": "On August 30, 2026, fictional Meridian Cooperative Bank records revealed a transfer of INR 485,000 from account ML-TEST-4401 to NL-TEST-7712, an account previously associated with Northstar Logistics Ltd. Subsequent surveillance observed Ravi Sen, an operations manager at Northstar Logistics Ltd., arriving at Meridian Warehouse in vehicle WB-99-TEST-091. Later, a white Falcon Courier hatchback (WB-99-TEST-204) entered East Dock Storage Unit 4, a new storage facility. Neel Arora, identified as the operator of East Dock Storage Unit 4, was linked to phone number +91-90000-10093. A meeting between Neel Arora and Ravi Sen occurred near the storage facility, followed by a 176-second phone call between +91-90000-10092 and +91-90000-10093. The WB-99-TEST-204 then departed East Dock Storage Unit 4. This intelligence adds new entities and locations to the ongoing CASE-0091 investigation, corroborating earlier activity and suggesting a coordinated network.",
